  "notes": "Theatrical art-pop with an alto lead and a literary lyric register. The drums are authored from a two-mode claim with one shared behaviour: \"piano-led tracks use a plain kick/snare with tom fills; the electropop mode uses a gated snare, hard clap and 8th synth pulse. Percussion serves the theatrical cadence, stopping dead for spoken lines.\" That stopping-dead is `kick.beatSkipProb` 0.24 and a perc density that reaches 0, which is a different device from the other quiet models in this section — the silence here is a cadence, not a texture. The bass is explicitly not an 808: \"synth or electric bass on roots with an octave-jump habit; low end absent in the piano-only passages\", so the cell shapes carry the octave and no `bass808` block exists. Harmony is the entry's own: \"minor keys with chromatic passing chords and a wide use of the major-III as a brightening device\", so III is in two families and `susOrDimProb` is raised to carry the chromatic passing colour. \"Piano is the writing instrument, so voicings are close triads with an active left hand\" is `voicing.style` close with a high `triad` share. The melody block encodes \"wide-interval and declamatory with abrupt register switches, and the hook is often a spoken-shouted phrase\" as the highest `leap` share and the highest `octaveJumpProb` in this batch over an alto-low register; \"choral self-harmonies at cadences\" is the `sustain_pad` counter. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says \"tempo/harmony bands inferred\": every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the harmonic weights and `bpm.mode` 110 (the midpoint of the stated 90—130 band) are INFERRED. ⚠ The entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the contralto/head-voice claim is repeated here.",
